Description: Provides an interactive platform for statistical analysis
    of agricultural and biological experiments through a 'shiny'
    application in Brazilian Portuguese. The application is launched
    using run_app() and offers an accessible graphical interface
    for experimental data analysis and interpretation.
 .
    Features include data import, validation and exploratory analysis;
    analysis of variance for completely randomized, randomized
    complete block and factorial designs; and assessment of
    statistical assumptions using Shapiro-Wilk and Bartlett tests.
 .
    Multiple comparison procedures include Tukey-Kramer,
    Student-Newman-Keuls, Fisher's LSD, Scott-Knott, Dunnett,
    Bonferroni and Holm adjustments, with compact letter displays
    following Piepho (2004) <doi:10.1198/1061860043515>.
 .
    Regression tools support linear, polynomial, nonlinear and
    binomial models, confidence bands, model selection using
    information criteria described by Akaike (1974)
    <doi:10.1109/TAC.1974.1100705>, and estimation of
    agronomically optimal doses.
 .
    Additional methods include nonparametric tests
    (Kruskal-Wallis, Friedman, Mood's median and Dunn),
    classical and bootstrap confidence intervals based on
    Efron (1987) <doi:10.1080/01621459.1987.10478410>,
    principal component analysis, clustering and
    correlation analysis.
 .
    The application also provides a graphical editor,
    publication-quality figure export, and generation of
    results in 'Excel', HTML and 'Word' formats, including
    reproducible R scripts. Each module includes practical
    examples to support learning and application.
 .
    Documentation and a comprehensive user guide in
    Portuguese are available on the package website.
 .
